\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S3}{\ignorespaces \textbf {Functional annotations of key developmental markers.} Annotations compiled from UniProt, GeneCards, and literature review. All listed genes show conserved developmental expression patterns between pig and human muscle tissue. FC = log$_2$ fold change (adult/infant); positive values indicate higher expression in adults (upregulated during development), negative values indicate higher expression in infants (downregulated during development). Pig FC derived from pig GTEx data (GEO: GSE257558) \blx@tocontentsinit {0}\parencite {teng_compendium_2024}; Human FC from \blx@tocontentsinit {0}\textcite {schaiter_molecular_2024}.}}{125}{table.caption.21}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S4}{\ignorespaces \textbf {Stage-by-stage expression trajectories of key developmental markers.} Mean TPM values across porcine developmental stages for genes with conserved pig-human developmental patterns. Stage boundaries: Infant (0--20 days), Early childhood (21--59 days), Pre-pubertal (60--149 days), Post-pubertal (150--365 days), Adult (>365 days). ``Peak Change'' indicates the developmental transition with the largest fold change.}}{126}{table.caption.22}%
